issues.fix_hint:
Add a positive control to the same test so it fails if the reasoner stops running on this input. Cheapest option: seed a fact that OWL-RL is required to derive, and assert it alongside the two negative assertions. For example declare a subproperty and assert the derived edge:

    let q = ex(&mut dict, "q");
    let sub_prop = dict.intern_iri(&format!("{RDFS}subPropertyOf"));
    let mut triples = vec![
        [p, ty, reflexive],
        [p, sub_prop, q],
        [x, p, y],
    ];
    materialize_owl_rl(&mut dict, &mut triples);
    // positive control: the reasoner actually ran
    assert!(has(&dict, &set, "http://ex/x", "http://ex/q", "http://ex/y"), "rdfs7 control");
    // the guard proper
    assert!(!set.contains(&[x, p, x]), "OWL-RL must not derive a reflexive edge for :x");

Use whatever subPropertyOf/RDFS helper the surrounding test module already provides rather than introducing a new one.
